WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
The Third Plate

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
Seconds

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.310
Alice?!

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.860
What's wrong, Alice?

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.190
Erina, what are you waiting for?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.950
We're getting you out of here!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:13.910
What?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:21.870
<i>Nakiri Erina ran away from home for 
the first time in her life last night.</i>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.210
Run away!

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.630
In situations like these, normal boys 
and girls run away from home!

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.090
<i>She had nowhere to go, but she found a home.</i>

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.890
That's right.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.310
I came to the Polar Star Dormitory...

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.310
Nakiri-san!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.310
Huh?

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.270
Wow, you ran away from home, huh?

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.650
Nice, nice.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.070
You're not too shabby, Nakiri!

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.280
Don't make fun of me!

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.820
Let's play a card game!

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.610
Yeah!

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.530
Cards?!

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.580
<i>I haven't woken up feeling 
so light-hearted in a while.</i>

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.120
<i>Hey!</i>

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.580
<i>Who used up all the breakfast</i>

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.210
ingredients?!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.960
Oh, I used them... for last night's party.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.590
I used some, too, to serve 
to the God Tongue.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.380
I took some, too—just a little bit.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.550
I took the cured mackerel,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.850
but I braised it in greens 
and strawberry jam,

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.810
so you can serve it for breakfast.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.770
The hell I would!

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>You all take responsibility 
and make breakfast today!</i>

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.810
<i>You've got thirty minutes!</i>

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:30.650
<i>Okay!</i>

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>I'll go get some vegetables from the garden.</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.070
<i>I'll make a rice bowl using rice juice.</i>

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.530
<i>Maybe I'll cook Shikao's antlers.</i>

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.450
<i>I'm gonna make tempura with just 
the batter made from flour.</i>

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.160
<i>It tastes better if you use potato starch.</i>

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.240
<i>Don't mess with me!</i>

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>What'd you say?!</i>

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:49.130
<i>Can the genteel Erina survive in 
the chaotic Polar Star Dormitory?</i>

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.330
<i>Maybe I'll trot out my special smoked stuff.</i>

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:49.130
<i></i>Rocky said it's good for the 
health to swallow 24 eggs whole.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.250
<i>One calamari milkshake coming right up!</i>

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.650
The Third Plate

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.770
Food Wars

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.180
Erina at Polar Star Dormitory

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.180
Thanks for the food!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.140
Hey, that wasn't so bad 
for a slap-dash breakfast.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.270
Of course.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.900
We're Polar Star residents. We strike 
terror into the hearts of men.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.280
We managed to wing it with vegetables 
from the Polar Star garden, huh.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.240
But was it appropriate as the first 
breakfast for the God Tongue?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.080
Erinacchi, how was breakfast?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.620
Don't mind me.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.080
I enjoyed it—

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.210
other than curiosities like 
the small dried sardines

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.960
sauteed in mint sauce and cilantro.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.710
Oh, hey, Nakiri. That was good, wasn't it?

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.130
As if I'd even try an abomination like that!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.590
But the mackerel tossed in jam you 
served yesterday was a little tasty.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.600
I still would've preferred that 
he not spread it on toast, though.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.890
Don't hold back.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:08.470
I'm not!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.470
Don't make anyone but Megumi into a victim!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.520
What?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:17.480
Laundry Room

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.860
I narrowly escaped becoming 
Yukihira-kun's guinea pig.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.190
Laundry Room

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>The laundry room...</i>

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.200
Hm?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.910
<i>It's very different from the 
laundry room back home.</i>

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.660
<i>I guess this isn't my family's estate.</i>

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.620
<i>I should do my own laundry.</i>

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.660
<i>There are so many buttons!</i>

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.500
<i>How does this thing even work?</i>

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.500
<i>I'm sure the detergent goes somewhere...</i>

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.000
<i>I wonder if the water just 
comes out automatically...</i>

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.550
Oh, Nakiri.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.590
Yukihira-kun!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.680
You're already doing laundry when 
you just got here yesterday?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.640
Nothing gets by you, huh?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.550
Er, I guess.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.560
Well, I like doing laundry, too.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.930
<i>Which button is he going to push?</i>

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.560
Huh? What?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.770
Nothing.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.940
Oh, right. This must be your 
first time in this room, Nakiri.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.110
Y-Yes.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:08.070
Do you want me to tell you how 
if you have any questions?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.500
But I guess you'd be able to use 
something like a washing machine.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.120
O-O-O-O-O-Of course!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.790
D-D-Don't make fun of me!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.540
Right, right. Sorry.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.000
Oh.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>How dare he?!</i>

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.590
<i>Of course I can figure out laundry on my own!</i>

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.510
<i>Just watch!</i>

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.170
<i>Um, er...</i>

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.470
Oh, Nakiri-san?

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.970
Oh, hello.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.180
What are you doing here, Erinacchi?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.390
But I guess that's obvious.
 You're doing laundry.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.100
I guess one machine's taken.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.600
Nakiri-san, do you mind if we share?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.100
Huh?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.230
We always do our laundry in the same machine.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.440
It's more efficient that way.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.240
I see.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.110
I suppose... I could...

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.080
Make sure you separate out 
anything that might bleed.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:51.990
<i>"Bleed"?</i>

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.990
Make sure you presoak 
stains in bleach solution.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:54.950
<i>"Presoak"?</i>

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.960
I'm going to put these into nets, okay?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.250
<i>The world of laundry is so complex.</i>

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:06.470
<i>Nakiri Erina was caught up in the
maelstrom of culture shock.</i>

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:12.260
<i>I managed to do laundry with help 
from Tadokoro-san and the others.</i>

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.440
You know, I thought Erina-chan was 
a superhuman who could do everything,

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.230
but I bet she's actually not really 
good at household chores and stuff.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.190
She's way different from how she looks.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.320
Okay, Ryo-kun, let's go!

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.360
Huh? Go where?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:35.290
Oh, c'mon! Of course we're going to 
Polar Star Dormitory to check on Erina!

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.790
But isn't that supposed to be a secret?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.500
Of course it is.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.380
We have to make sure
 Uncle Azami never finds out.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.380
But, Miss...

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.460
If we go there in a huge 
stretch limo like this,

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.930
I think it'll be super obvious.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.720
Oh, you're right.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.390
Okay, let's go in a short limo.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.810
That wasn't my point.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.770
Tadokoro Megumi...

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.900
Over here, Tadokoro Megumi.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:10.360
Huh?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.320
It's me.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.320
Don't raise your voice.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.910
Arato-san? What are you doing?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.290
There may be spies sent 
by Azami-dono hereabouts.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.710
Don't act suspicious.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.500
I think you're the one acting suspicious.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.250
Don't talk!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.040
Don't tense up!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:25.840
Huh, um, er?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.210
Don't shake!

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.210
Don't panic!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.050
Don't go pale!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.510
What's wrong, Hisako?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.050
Erina-sama,

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:38.020
I felt you must be feeling discomfort due 
to the sudden departure from your home,

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.140
so I brought a care package.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.980
In it are a toothbrush and
 changes of clothing, of course,

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.650
as well as a body pillow to help you rest...

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.810
It smells nice.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.360
...a blanket made from 
high-quality materials...

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.440
It's very soft.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:53.530
Baby Animals

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.740
...a photo book of baby 
animals to help you relax...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.530
They're so plush.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:58.040
<i>One medicinal dish, two medicinal dishes,
 three medicinal dishes...</i>

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:57.240
...and a relaxation CD to help you de-stress.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.700
It sounds very sleepy.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:03.870
When You Wish Upon a Star

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:02.670
And even the newest work from the 
author of that manga you like!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.870
Thank you, Hisako.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.750
<i>Is this what running away from 
home supposed to be like?</i>

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.170
Look sharp, everyone!

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.760
Today's cleaning day!

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.340
Oh, right.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.720
I'll do the hallways.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.260
I'll deal with the grime in the kitchen.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.300
I'll do the bathroom.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.640
I'm the one on bathroom duty this month.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.270
You do the toilet.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.680
You do the toilet, you shithead.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.020
I do the bath.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.600
It's <i>my</i> bath.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.810
You two do both, together!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:27.560
Yes'm.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.020
Cleaning day?

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.150
Yeah, we have it once a month.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.030
Sorry for the ruckus.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.320
It'll be over soon, so just relax.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.950
Nakiri-chan can't do any 
household chores, huh.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.660
It's not what you'd expect,
 since she acts like a know-it-all.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.670
Um!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.540
May I join in the cleaning?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.050
After all, you're letting 
me stay at this dorm.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.470
Erina-sama! I'll help, too.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.630
I'll do anything you tell me to.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.720
Okay.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.430
Thanks for your help, then.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.600
Arato-san, help me clean the back entrance.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.350
Got it.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.980
Nakiri-san, the entrance hall 
should be a good choice.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.440
I already moved the vacuum 
cleaner there, so it'll be easy.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.770
Um, vacuum cleaner?

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.650
Very well!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.000
<i>It's a bit different from what 
I've seen at the estate.</i>

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.960
<i>Hm, what's this symbol?</i>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.880
What impressive cutting-edge technology.

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.210
There.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.840
Perfect!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.800
I'm going to clean now!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.270
Hmm, is this how it's supposed to be?

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.230
I feel like something's missing.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.980
What're you up to, Nakiri?

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.650
C-Can't you tell?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.440
I'm vacuuming, okay?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.940
Without turning it on?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.650
I-I-I-I-I know!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.650
Th-Th-This is just visualization training!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.870
I'm t-t-t-training to vacuum 
efficiently, with precision!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:04.160
Oh, that thing Mimasaka does a lot, huh.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.830
Good day!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.710
High
Medium
Low

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.960
<i>Here's the power switch!</i>

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.840
<i>That's right!</i>

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.630
<i>This is how it's supposed to go!</i>

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.510
Well? Do you have any other complaints?

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.260
Uh, I didn't have any 
complaints to start with.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.220
I guess you're doing all right.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.480
This may all seem pretty strange,

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.890
but good luck.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.070
Thank you.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:39.200
Usayo, Kamomaru, Shikao, 
Inotaro, and everyone else—

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.660
Stay!

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.120
A wild game parade?!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.120
Erina, I came to check in on you!

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.460
What's this?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.130
I'm so sorry, Erinacchi!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.170
Oh, my, Erina.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.760
You're already having so 
much fun with your friends.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.390
I don't think that's what's going on.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:08.100
<i>The proud queen of the academy 
had become covered in dust.</i>

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.850
<i>Hang in there, Erina.</i>

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.560
<i>Don't let this get to you, Erina.</i>

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.980
Erina
at Polar Star Dormitory

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.940
Hey!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:21.950
I told you to clean the bathroom,
 not destroy it!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.160
Sorry!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.530
We'll fix it up straight away!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:25.990
So...

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.790
...we can't use our dorm's baths right now.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.830
Oh well.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.460
Yeah!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.830
So this is a public bath?

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.790
It's not like a ryokan.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:39.800
Public baths have been used by common folk 
since the Edo period on a daily basis.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.550
In other words, for someone of 
noble birth like Erina-sama, it...

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:48.020
Mt. Tenno

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.800
...would not be hyperbole to 
say it will be her Mt. Tenno!

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.020
Nah, that's hyperbole.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.890
Mt. Tenno? A mountain?

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:54.520
It's an old expression for a watershed 
moment that defines victory or defeat.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.520
That might be exaggerating it a bit.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.440
Hey, I'm getting all itchy from 
the dust. Let's go already.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.450
Bath

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.530
Let us proceed, Erina-sama!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.450
All right.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:07.580
<i>Huh, it's pretty retro inside, too.</i>

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.700
They don't even have lockers 
in this day and age.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:13.580
Hey, they have coffee milk 
to drink after taking a dip, too!

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.330
Oh, hey, Takumi and Isami!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.920
What?! Yukihira?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.050
Oh, hello.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.920
Hey, I didn't expect to 
run into you two here.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.300
We like how they have a hotter bath here.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:28.640
We come here sometimes when we 
want to take a bath in a big one.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.890
You're instantly recharged.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:35.100
It's a self-care spot known to a select few.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.810
Huh, I had no idea.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:41.400
So maybe we'll run into someone else here.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.110
Well, we'll get going.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.570
This place is retro,
but there's even a sauna here.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:47.820
Take your time.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:48.830
Nice.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.370
<i>You can totally hear the
 conversations in the men's bath.</i>

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.290
Erina, you're taking your sweet time.

